r Heritage Speakers", "titleLong": "Spanish for Heritage Speakers", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "SEM", "ssrComponentLong": "Seminar", "section": "102", "classNbr": 6669, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "12:20PM", "timeEnd": "01:10PM", "startDt": "01/22/2024", "endDt": "05/07/2024", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 2, "netid": "mkr4", "firstName": "Mary", "middleName": "Kathryn", "lastName": "Redmond"}], "pattern": "MWF", "facilityDescr": "Goldwin Smith Hall 160", "bldgDescr": "Goldwin Smith Hall", "facilityDescrshort": "GSH160", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "01/22/2024", "endDt": "05/18/2024", "addConsent": "N", "addConsentDescr": "No Special Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "P", "instrModeDescrshort": "In Person", "instrModeDescr": "In Person", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "O", "exploreCriteriaIds": [], "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 3, "unitsMaximum": 3, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["SEM"], "gradingBasis": "GRD", "gradingBasisShort": "Graded", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter grades only", "simpleCombinations": [{"subject": "SPAN", "catalogNbr": "2000", "type": "C"}], "sessionCode": "1", "sessionBeginDt": "01/22/2024", "sessionEndDt": "05/18/2024", "sessionLong": "Regular Academic Session", "exploreCriteriaIds": []}], "description": "Designed to expand bilingual Heritage students' knowledge of Spanish by providing them with ample opportunities to develop and improve each of the basic language skills, with a particular focus on writing vocabulary. The heritage student has at least one parent of Hispanic origin and grew up speaking Spanish at home; s/he also finished high school here in the US. After this course, students may take SPAN 2095.", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "Satisfies Option 1.", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Fall, Spring.", "catalogComments": "Students should speak with the instructor about their language skills and course placement.", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "Prerequisite: LSP 56 or higher, CASE placement.", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AS", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2867, "crseId": 368901, "crseOfferNbr": 2, "subject": "LSP", "catalogNbr": "2152", "titleShort": "(Im)migration and (Im)migrants", "titleLong": "(Im)migration and (Im)migrants: Then and Now", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 18619, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "11:40AM", "timeEnd": "12:55PM", "startDt": "01/22/2024", "endDt": "05/07/2024", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "fev2", "firstName": "Fernando", "middleName": "Enrique", "lastName": "Villegas Rivera"}], "pattern": "MW", "facilityDescr": "Rockefeller Hall 132", "bldgDescr": "Rockefeller Hall", "facilityDescrshort": "RCK132", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "01/22/2024", "endDt": "05/18/2024", "addConsent": "I", "addConsentDescr": "Instructor Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "P", "instrModeDescrshort": "In Person", "instrModeDescr": "In Person", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "O", "exploreCriteriaIds": [], "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 3, "unitsMaximum": 3, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["LEC"], "gradingBasis": "OPT", "gradingBasisShort": "Stdnt Opt", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter or S/U grades", "simpleCombinations": [{"subject": "AMST", "catalogNbr": "2152", "type": "C"}, {"subject": "GOVT", "catalogNbr": "2152", "type": "C"}], "sessionCode": "1", "sessionBeginDt": "01/22/2024", "sessionEndDt": "05/18/2024", "sessionLong": "Regular Academic Session", "exploreCriteriaIds": []}], "description": "How are migration dynamics produced? How do states and communities respond to and shape complex migration processes? This course will draw on the United States as a case study, focusing on Latino immigrants. Latinos are by far the largest immigrant group in the U.S., representing about 50% of all immigrants. Additionally, the U.S. has historically received the largest number of immigrants in the world. The class will examine the main debates around migration in fields such as Latino studies, migration studies, and political science. We begin with a historical and contemporary survey of global and regional migration trends. Next, we will review theories explaining why people migrate and how countries manage migration processes. We then focus on the U.S. immigration apparatus, examining past and present changes, including migration public policies. Central to this class is the exploration of multiple systems of marginalization that shape the opportunities, material conditions, and lived experiences of immigrants in the U.S. We conclude with an exploration of historical and contemporary migrant-led forms of resistance, such as the Immigrant Rights Movement, and its linkages to other transnational struggles for social justice.", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "(SBA-AS, SCD-AS)", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Spring.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AS", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2867, "crseId": 372875, "crseOfferNbr": 2, "subject": "LSP", "catalogNbr": "3215", "titleShort": "Performance and Immigration", "titleLong": "Performance and Immigration:Staging the Migrant, Alien, and Refugee in and outside the US", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 19840, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "11:40AM", "timeEnd": "12:55PM", "startDt": "01/22/2024", "endDt": "05/07/2024", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "jma377", "firstName": "Juan", "middleName": "Manuel", "lastName": "Aldape Munoz"}], "pattern": "MW", "facilityDescr": "Schwartz Ctr-Perform Arts 124", "bldgDescr": "Schwartz Ctr-Performing Arts", "facilityDescrshort": "SWZ124", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "01/22/2024", "endDt": "05/18/2024", "addConsent": "N", "addConsentDescr": "No Special Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "P", "instrModeDescrshort": "In Person", "instrModeDescr": "In Person", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "O", "exploreCriteriaIds": [], "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 3, "unitsMaximum": 3, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["LEC"], "gradingBasis": "GRD", "gradingBasisShort": "Graded", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter grades only", "simpleCombinations": [{"subject": "PMA", "catalogNbr": "3215", "type": "C"}], "sessionCode": "1", "sessionBeginDt": "01/22/2024", "sessionEndDt": "05/18/2024", "sessionLong": "Regular Academic Session", "exploreCriteriaIds": []}], "description": "In this course, we interrogate how immigration debates are staged and experiences of belonging are redefined through performance. The categories of \"undocumented,\" \"illegal,\" \"displaced,\" and \"exile\" collide on international and national stages when governmental bodies decide who gets to be a migrant and under what terms. We assess how bodies marked culturally and legally as \"aliens\" use performance to navigate complex migration laws and dangerous social terrains that appear to be shifting and solidifying at the same time. We consider performances on stage, as well as performance in a broader understanding. We examine visual, linguistic, and performative representations of migrant experiences. We analyze and write about performances that deal with issues of migration beyond economic and security models.", "catalogBreadth": null, "catalogDistr": null, "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": null, "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": null, "catalogAttribute": null, "catalogWhenOffered": null, "catalogComments": null, "catalogPrereqCoreq": null, "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": null, "catalogSatisfiesReq": null, "catalogPermission": null, "catalogCourseSubfield": null, "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AS", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2867, "crseId": 350954, "crseOfferNbr": 2, "subject": "LSP", "catalogNbr": "3551", "titleShort": "Modern, Contemp Latin Amer Art", "titleLong": "Modern and Contemporary Latin American Art", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 18561, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "10:10AM", "timeEnd": "11:25AM", "startDt": "01/22/2024", "endDt": "05/07/2024", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "mf252", "firstName": "Maria", "middleName": "", "lastName": "Fernandez"}], "pattern": "MW", "facilityDescr": "Goldwin Smith Hall G24", "bldgDescr": "Goldwin Smith Hall", "facilityDescrshort": "GSHG24", "meetingTopicDescription": ""